  "title": "Victory at Endor",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 9 of 10",
  "description": "\"Horror Beyond Imagination\" sounds like anything but Star Wars, so when producers of Return of the Jedi made plans for filming, they took curious but necessary precautions to avoid publicity. They deliberately misidentified their project as a scary movie called Blue Harvest, using the above tagline to throw fans off the scent. This ruse has been credited to producer Howard Kazanjian, and the campaign was very thorough, emblazoning the fictitious film's logo on a wide range of production items including shirts, caps, coats, buttons, signs, invoices and stationery. The only tip to the trick was the supposed films logo, which, perhaps unintentionally, utilized the distinctive Star Wars lettering style."
}
